+# BatchBeacon Impeccable reference guidance
+
+Modified on 18 October 2026 from Paul Bakaus's Apache-2.0 Impeccable 4.6.0,
+commit 08d5b470495d242ca0470f4aeae1956c3a074f83. This is an explicitly adapted
+text-only subset. See PROVENANCE.md, LICENSE and NOTICE.md. It is not the upstream
+executable workflow and makes no detector, hook or engine execution claim.
+
+Read PRODUCT.md and the project's approved requirements first. Use the native
+code-first Operate path. Read reference/init.md, reference/new-work.md,
+reference/operate.md, reference/mode-operate.md and reference/craft-floor.md.
+No launcher, binary, catalog request, live server, telemetry, hook, nested agent,
+automatic asset work or external provider is included or authorized by this skill.
+
+The accepted A workflow and recorded decisions take precedence. Do not repeat a
+stack/interview/direction tournament. Produce a materially improved workbench,
+retail queue and guidance lifecycle with actual source facts and explicitly
+synthetic shop/evidence content. Preserve all three earlier UI directions.
+
+Use standard HTML controls, Jinja and CSS. Keep the next user action clear;
+show unknown, expired, historical, stale and failed states without implying
+clearance. Readable density and familiar affordances beat decoration.
+
+Apply Emil selectively to touch, focus, interruptibility and reduced motion.
+Operate rules override decorative motion, custom scrollbars, staggered entry,
+React/Motion examples and gesture-only confirmation. Keyboard actions respond
+immediately. No extra runtime dependency is implied.
+
+Inspect actual 1440px and 390px renders and working state transitions. Report
+reproduced defects using project triage; taste advice alone is not a release
+blocker. Keep prototype notes provisional. Final DESIGN.md and final visual
+integration remain behind the owner's concrete replacement-treatment approval.
